       | \]
       | 
       | and obtain  
       | 
       | \[
       | (S_{n}\alpha)\star\beta=
       | \begin{cases}
       | 1,& n=k\text{ or }n=k+d,\\[2pt]
       | 0,&\text{otherwise}.
       | \end{cases}
       | \]
       | 
       | Thus every listed \(\alpha\) is indeed shifty, and the classification shows
       | that no other \(\alpha\) can satisfy the required condition.
