       | returns to its original value.  
       | In those 12 steps the first hand moves east exactly \(w\) times and the second
       | hand moves north \(12-w\) times, so the net displacement after a block of 12
       | steps is the vector  
       | 
       | \[
       | v=(w,\;12-w)\in\mathbb Z_{12}\times\mathbb Z_{12}.
       | \]
       | 
       | Repeating the block \(t\) times moves us by \(t\,v\).  
       | The orbit of any vertex therefore has length  
       | 
       | \[
       | L=12\cdot\operatorname{ord}(v),
       | \]
       | 
       | where \(\operatorname{ord}(v)\) is the additive order of \(v\) in
       | \(\mathbb Z_{12}^2\).  
       | Because \(12-w\equiv -w\pmod{12}\), the order of \(v\) equals the order of
       | \(w\) in the cyclic group \(\mathbb Z_{12}\), namely  
       | 
       | \[
       | \operatorname{ord}(v)=\frac{12}{\gcd(w,12)} .
       | \]
       | 
