       | \[
       | \mathcal F=\{\,\overline{PQ}\mid P=(p,0),\;Q=(0,q),\;p,q\ge 0,\;p^{2}+q^{2}=1 \,\}.
       | \]
       | 
       | For a member \(\overline{PQ}\) with \(P=(t,0)\;(0<t\le 1)\) we have  
       | 
       | \[
       | q=\sqrt{1-t^{2}},\qquad 
       | \text{equation of }\overline{PQ}:\; y=-\frac{q}{t}x+q .
       | \tag{1}
       | \]
       | 
       | The line \(\overline{AB}\) is  
       | 
       | \[
       | y=-\sqrt3\,x+\frac{\sqrt3}{2}. \tag{2}
       | \]
       | 
       | ---
       | 
       | ### Intersection of a segment of \(\mathcal F\) with \(\overline{AB}\)
       | 
       | Equating (1) and (2) gives the abscissa of their intersection:
       | 
       | \[
       | -\sqrt3\,x+\frac{\sqrt3}{2}= -\frac{q}{t}x+q
       | \Longrightarrow
       | x=\frac{q-\frac{\sqrt3}{2}}{\frac{q}{t}-\sqrt3},
       | \qquad q=\sqrt{1-t^{2}}. \tag{3}
       | \]
       | 
       | Define  
       | 
       | \[
       | x(t)=\frac{\sqrt{1-t^{2}}-\frac{\sqrt3}{2}}{\frac{\sqrt{1-t^{2}}}{t}-\sqrt3},
       | \qquad 0<t<1,\;t\neq\frac12 .
       | \]
       | 
       | ---
       | 
       | ### Behaviour of \(x(t)\)
       | 
       | * As \(t\to 0^{+}\): \(\;x(t)\to 0\).
       | * As \(t\to 1^{-}\): \(\;x(t)\to\frac12\).
       | * As \(t\to\frac12\) from either side the denominator of (3) tends to \(0\); using the limit  
