       | assistantfinalLet the three edge vectors of a parallelepiped be \(\mathbf a ,\mathbf b ,\mathbf c\).
       | All faces are rhombi, so for each pair of edges the two edges have the same
       | length.  
       | Hence  
       | 
       | \[
       | |\mathbf a|=|\mathbf b|=|\mathbf c|=:s .
       | \]
       | 
       | For a rhombus the diagonals are \(\mathbf u+\mathbf v\) and \(\mathbf u-\mathbf v\)
       | when the sides are \(\mathbf u,\mathbf v\).  
       | Their lengths are  
       | 
       | \[
       | |\mathbf u+\mathbf v|^{2}=2s^{2}+2\mathbf u\!\cdot\!\mathbf v,\qquad
       | |\mathbf u-\mathbf v|^{2}=2s^{2}-2\mathbf u\!\cdot\!\mathbf v .
       | \]
       | 
       | Each face has diagonal lengths \(\sqrt{21}\) and \(\sqrt{31}\); therefore for
       | every unordered pair \(\{\mathbf u,\mathbf v\}\)
       | 
       | \[
       | \{\,2s^{2}+2\mathbf u\!\cdot\!\mathbf v,\;2s^{2}-2\mathbf u\!\cdot\!\mathbf v\,\}
       |    =\{21,31\}.
       | \]
       | 
       | Thus  
       | 
       | \[
       | 2s^{2}=26\quad\Longrightarrow\quad s^{2}=13\;(s=\sqrt{13}),
       | \]
       | and  
       | 
       | \[
       | \mathbf u\!\cdot\!\mathbf v=\pm\frac52 .
       | \]
       | 
       | Denote  
       | 
       | \[
       | p=\mathbf a\!\cdot\!\mathbf b,\qquad q=\mathbf a\!\cdot\!\mathbf c,
       | \qquad r=\mathbf b\!\cdot\!\mathbf c,
       | \]
       | each equal to \(\pm\frac52\).
       | 
       | The Gram matrix of \(\mathbf a,\mathbf b,\mathbf c\) is  
       | 
       | \[
       | G=\begin{pmatrix}
       | 13&p&q\\[2pt]
       | p&13&r\\[2pt]
       | q&r&13
       | \end{pmatrix}.
       | \]
       | 
       | Its determinant equals the square of the volume \(V\) of the parallelepiped:
       | 
       | \[
       | \det G = 13^{3}+2pqr-13(p^{2}+q^{2}+r^{2})
       |        =2197-13\!\left(\frac{25}{4}\cdot3\right)+2pqr
       |        =\frac{7813+125\,\sigma}{4},
       | \]
       | 
