       | 13 & \frac52\varepsilon_{12} & \frac52\varepsilon_{13}\\[2pt]
       | \frac52\varepsilon_{12} & 13 & \frac52\varepsilon_{23}\\[2pt]
       | \frac52\varepsilon_{13} & \frac52\varepsilon_{23} & 13
       | \end{pmatrix}.
       | \]
       | 
       | For a symmetric \(3\times3\) matrix with equal diagonal entries \(a\) and off‑diagonal entries \(x,y,z\),
       | 
       | \[
       | \det = a^{3}+2xyz-a(x^{2}+y^{2}+z^{2}).
       | \]
       | 
       | Here \(a=13\) and \(x=\frac52\varepsilon_{12},\;y=\frac52\varepsilon_{13},\;z=\frac52\varepsilon_{23}\).
       | Since \(\varepsilon_{ij}^{2}=1\),
